      "refersTo": "destination-selected",
      "description": "Quiet baseline with a soft current destination and wrapping phone labels.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabs\"><button class=\"ds-tab\" aria-current=\"page\">Activité</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">À suivre</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Réglages</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;padding:0 0 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--work-line,#dedfe3)}.ds-tab{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI Variable\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;min-height:44px;min-width:0;padding:10px 18px;border:0;border-radius:8px;background:transparent;color:var(--work-muted,#62656d);font-size:14px;font-weight:550;cursor:pointer}.ds-tab[aria-current],.ds-tab:hover{background:var(--work-soft,#f0f1f3);color:var(--work-ink,#202125)}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--work-accent,#286047);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:860px){.ds-tabs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:4px}.ds-tab{min-height:46px;padding:10px 3px;font-size:13px;white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Filter chips",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "filter-selected",
      "description": "A pressed filter uses a soft fill while unpressed filters remain quiet.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-filters\" aria-label=\"Filtrer\"><button class=\"ds-filter\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Tout</button><button class=\"ds-filter\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Factures</button><button class=\"ds-filter\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Règles</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;min-width:0}.ds-filter{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI Variable\", \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:550;padding:8px 12px;min-height:44px;border:0;border-radius:8px;background:transparent;color:var(--work-muted,#62656d);cursor:pointer}.ds-filter[aria-pressed='true']{background:var(--work-soft,#f0f1f3);color:var(--work-ink,#202125)}.ds-filter:hover:not(:disabled){filter:brightness(.94)}.ds-filter:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--work-accent,#286047);outline-offset:3px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.ds-filter{transition:background-color 160ms ease-out,color 160ms ease-out}}@media(max-width:380px){.ds-filter{padding-inline:8px;font-size:12px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Grouped panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "content-panel",
      "description": "Flat, bordered group; nested records share its surface.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2 class=\"ds-title\">Projets</h2><p class=\"ds-copy\">Les informations de votre entreprise.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI Variable\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--work-line,#dedfe3);border-radius:12px;background:var(--work-paper,#ffffff);color:var(--work-ink,#202125);box-shadow:none}.ds-title{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-copy{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--work-muted,#62656d)}@media(max-width:860px){.ds-panel{padding:20px 16px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "One Working Window",
    "overview": "A restrained Apple-inspired working window: pearl-gray navigation, a continuous near-white canvas, graphite text and fine separators. Green identifies action and meaningful selection; the established Zentra wordmark remains the identity. Dark appearance preserves the same structure with distinct graphite surfaces.\n\nThis records the implemented shared screen layer across the application and its portal forms. It replaces the earlier Automation-only visual specification. The [workspace surface contract](.impeccable/surfaces/workspace.md) owns dashboard composition and module-specific arrangements; [PRODUCT.md](PRODUCT.md) owns product behavior. Printed sales documents retain their own layout, identity and colors.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One continuous working canvas with a separate navigation rail.",
      "System typography, aligned numbers and readable records.",
      "Flat grouped content, small control corners and depth reserved for dialogs.",
      "Compact desktop controls and safe-area-aware touch layouts.",
      "Matching light and dark roles, visible focus and optional motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Functional Color Rule",
        "body": "Use green for action and meaningful selection, and preserve written status alongside every semantic color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Familiar Type Rule",
        "body": "Use the platform text family for the interface; financial values and time use tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tonal Depth Rule",
        "body": "Separate resting content through surface tone and fine lines. Reserve the shared ambient shadow for dialogs.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do switch all shared color roles together in light and dark appearance.",
      "Do use platform text and tabular numerals for values, time and counts.",
      "Do keep focus outlines, text labels and real state evidence visible.",
      "Do let translated titles and step labels wrap on narrow screens.",
      "Do retain safe-area insets, touch targets and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do apply the same field and action treatment inside portal forms.",
      "Do preserve printed document colors, identity and layout."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add decorative gradients, glass panels or fabricated activity indicators to the shared working canvas.",
      "Don't replace status text with color alone.",
      "Don't turn each record or paragraph into a floating card.",
      "Don't use compact desktop navigation dimensions for touch navigation.",
      "Don't apply screen color aliases globally to printed document templates."
    ]
  }
}
